index 0000000..2e6f487
--- /dev/null
+++ b/releasenotes/notes/fix-falsy-callable-wait-5c2e8d1f7a9b4e63.yaml
@@ -0,0 +1,8 @@
+---
+fixes:
+  - |
+    A callable ``wait`` strategy is now always called, even when it is falsy
+    (for example, an empty container or an object whose ``__bool__`` or
+    ``__len__`` returns False). Previously such a strategy was silently
+    skipped and retries happened with no delay. The sync and async retry
+    loops both honour this. ``None``, ``0`` and ``sum([])`` still mean no wait.
